module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "adding_a_seed_module_refuses_convergence_on_an_unowned_lib_rs" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: MechanicallyPreventable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the convergence planner and the lib.rs renderer both derive crate-root membership from the partition the run itself declares, so a PR that adds a seed module converges in one heal invocation with no generated file installed by hand beyond the module's FIRST mirror, whose install is a deliberate authorial act rather than a gap: the host refuses to admit an emitted-but-uncommitted surface because an authored module and an emitter that invented a surface produce the same population (the emitted_not_committed arm of validate_compared_populations in required_regen_host.rs) -- DELIVERED 2026-11-12 by PR #16377 (the ppf-16377 receipt below), which also closed the boundary half. THE CAPABILITY THAT REMAINS FOR THE CEILING is that no compiled-in crate-root renderer should remain to be called at all: src/v1/stage0_crates.dag stage0_crate_plan_outcome is imported by src/v1/workspace_members.dag and has no call site anywhere, in .dag or in Rust; src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/emit_host.rs passes generated_partition_crate_rows() to the render for the fixture instrument and a required_regen_host test fixture does the same; dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_partition_package_graph.dag still defaults its two wrappers to generated_partition_crate_rows; and the partition-move admission has never been exercised UNDER THE DECLARED FOLD: admit_derived_partition_move, partition_move_explanation_child and boundary_fold sit behind the WholeCompilerRebuildRequired PartitionGenerationAuthorityChanged arm, which needs a stage to move a mirror named in data rebuild_scope_partition_generation_mirrors -- the two paths gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs and v1_compiler_stage0_crates.rs -- and no strict specimen has moved either, while the three historical runs that did fire that arm (ppx-16358, ppz-16358, jt5-16251) ran pre-#16373 code and so exercised the old admission rather than this fold. THE EXACT SPECIMEN THAT WOULD EXERCISE IT, agreed with bold-wren-111 in msg_e435a871 and deliberately NOT commissioned for this PR: the ppf construction plus the partition carrier .dag row in the change's own diff -- base = main + git revert of 2bcad60f --no-ff the fix, head = that base + the change's 8 authored files + the carrier .dag row, which is the original PR's file set minus only its hand-written mirror. A module moved inside the authored partition file alone would NOT fire the arm, because nothing in such a diff touches the carrier .dag and so the carrier .rs never moves. Each of those is a leaf someone could write against the snapshot again, so it is the guard standing there, not the absence of the snapshot, that keeps this class at mechanically preventable rather than structurally guaranteed",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL wave 1, PR #14317, 2026-10-18): the wave made std.host_text a dependency of seed-mirrored modules (std.coercion, gunbc.rust_crate_package_ident, extdeps.version.semver), so a new stage0 module std_host_text entered the seed. After the partition row and the produced mirror were committed, heal-generated-artifacts (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost`) still refused, printing only `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant Refused`. Exposing the planner's payload (a local, unpushed edit of v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_stage_plan_kind_label) read: SeedMembershipUnresolved { reason: lib.rs has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition, surface: RegenSurfaceIdentity { declaring_module: v1.compiler.emit_rust, projected_path: lib.rs } }. The lib.rs the candidate tree held was itself TRANSITIONAL: committing it got past the planner, but once the regenerated partition mirror was installed too, the candidate lib.rs no longer declared std_host_text (a partition crate owns it) and lib.rs returned to main's bytes -- so the planner refused twice on two different lib.rs states before either was the fixed point.",
    "WHAT ONE NEW SEED MODULE COST, IN ORDER, each a separate heal round and each a generator output installed outside the job that owns it: (1) the partition row (v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition) and the regenerated partition file; (2) the produced mirror std_host_text.rs (`emitted surface has no committed mirror`); (3) a transitional lib.rs (SeedMembershipUnresolved, above); (4) the partition file's own mirror gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs (`WholeCompilerRebuildRequired partition_generation_authority=[...]`); (5) lib.rs again, back to main's bytes; (6) the partition crate src/v1/stage0_std_core/src/lib.rs from `claim_executor --emit-partition-crates --write` (E0432 unresolved crate::std_host_text in the seed build). Every one is derivable from the partition row alone; heal derives none of them in one round.",
    "DEFECT 1 -- INVALID STATE: lib.rs, the stage0 crate's module list, is a seed surface the convergence planner must classify, but no row of gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_generated owns it, so the host derives UnresolvedSeedMembership for it (src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs, the `has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition` arm) and v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction regen_first_unresolved refuses the whole stage. Any change that adds or removes a seed module changes lib.rs, so EVERY such PR refuses convergence and needs lib.rs installed by hand from the candidate tree. HARM: the heal job cannot converge a routine seed-module addition; authors install generated files outside the job that owns them.",
    "DEFECT 2 -- INVALID STATE: the host's projection of the planner outcome (required_regen_host.rs, the `convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant <value>` arm, reading regen_stage_plan_kind_label) renders RegenStagePlanningRefused as the bare word `Refused`, dropping the RegenConvergenceRefusal payload that names the refusal and its surface. HARM: a typed, located refusal reaches CI as an unlocated one; the specimen cost three remote regen runs to read a reason the model already carried. This is gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed's `every degradation is typed, located and countable` lost at the last link.",
    "DEFECT 3 -- INVALID STATE: the heal step `Refuse when the stage0 round wrote a file the seed-build writer owns` (dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet) crashed in its own evaluation on #14317 at 7bf0694203a (2026-10-18): `error: evaluating heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet ... cause: NoSuchVariable { name: \"value\" }`. Its refusal message is built only on the drifted arm, from `map(drifted, d => d.entry.path.value as String)`, so the path it should name -- the seed-build roster file it found drifted -- never reaches CI. HARM: a typed, located refusal (`HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact`, naming the paths) becomes an evaluator crash with no subject; the author cannot tell which file, or whether the refusal fired at all. CEILING: structurally guaranteed (the refusal's rendering is total over its own carrier and is exercised by a control). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the overlap refusal renders every drifted path through an accessor the evaluator resolves, proved by a control that feeds a non-empty drifted population and expects the named paths in the reason.",
    "DEFECT 3 ROOT CAUSE, FOUND (2026-10-18, by bisecting #14317's 83 .dag changes on a 64 GB runner): the overlap step's crash was NOT the heal tool's -- it was THIS ROW. An earlier wording of the DEFECT 2 receipt quoted the host's format string with its placeholder in braces, and a braced identifier inside a .dag string literal is interpolation, so evaluating this module (which the overlap step's closure loads) looked up a variable named value and failed. Restoring this one file made the step exit 0; restoring any other changed file did not. The placeholder is now written with angle brackets. The step's crash therefore says nothing about heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet's own rendering, and DEFECT 3 above is withdrawn as a heal defect. What it does show is a separate hazard: a ledger row's prose can break an unrelated tool's evaluation, and the failure names the variable, not the file.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable for both -- the refusal is loud (the job fails), and a by-hand install of generator output works around defect 1; nothing mechanical prevents either. CEILING: structurally guaranteed for defect 1 (every seed surface the planner sees has an owner or a declared bootstrap role, so UnresolvedSeedMembership is unreachable for lib.rs) and for defect 2 (the planner's refusal crosses to the host as a typed value that the host renders whole).",
    "DEFECT 4 -- INVALID STATE, found by execution while measuring DEFECT 1's next rung (2026-11-12, my numbering; the row already holds a DEFECT 3 from 2026-10-18): a change that authors a stage0 module .dag plus its row in src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag, and nothing else, is refused in generation 0 - before any join, drift comparison or install - by a DIFFERENT admission, one whose rows come from a THIRD carrier the author never wrote. Verbatim, from the srv1 unit pp-16358 run by bold-wren-111 on a subject that is exactly that shape (a scratch stage0 module with a partition row and no other surface): `required-regen: refused: Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered: 3 emitted edge endpoint(s) have no stage0 crate (neither a module-bearing partition row nor the host shell lists them)` naming `v1_compiler_heal_missing_mirror_probe` three times (runtime-prelude, reexport-facade, declared-import), then `regen-round-cost: refused: rebuilt seed produced no fresh generation receipt at .../target/stage0-regen-receipt.json; status=exit status: 1`. Nothing was installed: git status empty, every sampled surface unchanged since 23:28:58Z, ordinal=0 only. WHY, read at 077460dff31f by eager-gull-72: that admission takes its rows from generated_partition_crate_rows evaluated from the GENERATED carrier dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_crate_partition_generated.dag, not from the authored src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag the author did write. Host side: required_regen_host emitted_tree_packages entered dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_emitted_edge_admission.dag under the regen source roots, resolved it with resolve_orchestrator_model, and decoded the carrier's generated_partition_crate_rows through the interpreter (what it does now, and what this classification changed, is in the receipt below); that model module imports that model module imports gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_generated at its line 16 and says at its lines 41 and 173 that it uses never the rows or shell edges compiled into the binary that asks. So the rows are read fresh from the corpus in hand - from the projection, not from the authority it projects. My first wording of this receipt said the rows came from the COMPILED mirror src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs; that was wrong, bold-wren-111 contradicted it from source (msg_f7d1a537) and I verified the contradiction rather than trusting it. What stands is the carrier and the ordering, not compiledness. For that subject the unit name appears twice in the authored carrier and zero times in either generated surface. Its producer runs LATER in the same round: required_regen_host built_seed_boundary_drift invokes claim_executor --emit-partition-crates and install_built_seed_boundary invokes it with --write, so the check refuses during the seed rebuild, before the step that would refresh the rows it needs. This is the same bootstrap shape as DEFECT 1 - a projection consulted where the change's own rows are the authority - one carrier earlier, and a THIRD reader of those rows. My first pass also named two more required_regen_host readers as remaining compiled-in runtime readers; I checked them before leaving that in and they are not - both sit inside #[test] fns in mod tests, in an_emit_that_refuses_hands_back_no_files and in assembled_seed_includes_foundation_and_layered_partitions_not_emit_consumer, where reading the built binary's own rows is the point of the test. The readers are now classified, by who evaluates them and whether a replacement partition is in flight; every fresh-authority one that can reach the declared partition WITHOUT breaking the seed's own compile was fixed by PR #16373, and the two that cannot are named there as the next PR rather than quietly reclassified as legitimate. LEGITIMATELY COMPILED-IN, left so: src/v1/compile.dag emit_from_artifact_plan and src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag emit_rust, where the BUILT SEED projects the partition it was built with and no replacement partition is in flight -- 05_emit_rust.dag states that discriminator for its own path -- the cli_run/emit_host.rs instrument for the same reason, and v1_consumer_census v1_partition_manifest_dependencies, a census of the committed tree, which has to agree with the manifests it joins; imports of GeneratedPartitionCrateRow that carry no rows are shape only. partition_crate_boundary_host.rs partition_package_names() was inspected and left: its only in-repo reference is a re-export in cli_run.rs and it has no caller, so it decides nothing today, and deleting an uncalled function is not this defect. FRESH-AUTHORITY, moved onto the fold: required_regen_host emitted_tree_packages, the edge admission's package graph, now asks gunbc.stage0.stage0_emitted_edge_admission stage0_emitted_tree_packages_as_declared; v1_compiler_stage0_crates stage0_crate_plan_outcome and stage0_crate_boundary_emit_outcome now ask gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_emit generated_partition_crate_rows_as_declared, for the reason that the boundary outcome WRITES the boundary files, so for it a replacement partition always is in flight -- recorded here, as the owning record for that reason, and not only beside the code; stage0_partition_rebuild_scope stage0_partition_rebuild_decision_today and stage0_partition_rebuild_excluded_today, whose reverse closure now follows partition_package_dependency_names_over over the rows it is closing over instead of re-reading the carrier per row; and gunbc_repo_repo_self_build repo_self_build_partition_crate_packages. All of them reach the authored rows through the one mapping gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_emit generated_partition_crate_row_from_authority, so the kind map has one home, and none of them falls back to rows compiled into the running binary. It is NOT the missing-mirror admission this row's next rung added; that admission never ran, so pp-16358 establishes nothing about it either way. Consequence for the capability this row wants: a change that also carries the generated carrier rows gets past it - which is how #16251 does, its diff touching dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_crate_partition_generated.dag (read-only) - and a change that authors only the partition row does not. So the end-to-end shape is unreachable until this reader is fixed too. EXECUTED ON A REAL SPECIMEN 2026-11-12, the stronger receipt: the srv1 unit ppy-16358, run by bold-wren-111 on #16251 itself with its hand-installed generated surfaces removed so only the authored row remains (rust_crate_partition.dag:446 carries v1_compiler_rest_cause_text, the generated carrier and its .rs mirror carry nothing). It refused in generation 0 - REGEN_START 00:32:45Z, REGEN_END 01:09:54Z, EXIT=1, ordinal=0, nothing installed, git status empty, every sampled surface unchanged since 00:24:31Z, no regen receipt written, and the missing-mirror admission never printing: `required-regen: refused: Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered: 5 emitted edge endpoint(s) have no stage0 crate (neither a module-bearing partition row nor the host shell lists them)` naming v1_compiler_rest_cause_text five times, its own two (runtime-prelude, reexport-facade) plus three from v1_compiler_emit_rust (declared-import, semantic-source-reference, inline-path-reference) because #16251's emitter really calls into the module. So this is DEFECT 4 on the shipped specimen and not only on my scratch probe, and the endpoint count grows with whatever the new module is wired to. The fix is the RULE, not the site: collect every reader of generated_partition_crate_rows() and of the stage0_crate_partition_generated carrier at a cited revision, keep as legitimately compiled-in only the ones where the BUILT SEED projects itself, and make every fresh-authority reader read the change's own rows, failing closed when they cannot be read, with no fallback to the compiled copy.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGERS, AS CAPABILITIES. Defect 1: the convergence planner classifies the stage0 crate's lib.rs (and any other crate-root surface the emitter writes) with a declared role and seed membership, so a PR that adds a seed module converges in heal with no hand-installed file -- proved by a fixture that adds one module and expects a planned stage, not a refusal. Defect 2: the host renders a RegenStagePlanningRefused outcome with its full RegenConvergenceRefusal payload (variant, reason, surface), proved by a control that feeds the projection a refusal and expects the payload in the printed reason. Routed by tidy-ant-251 to Manager 2."
    "DEFECT 1, MECHANISM LOCATED AND CLOSED (2026-11-11, PR #16310, head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f): the row named the symptom (lib.rs refused twice on two states) without the link. One rule has two readers, and both asked the copy of the partition compiled into the running seed while the same emission renders that partition's mirror off the corpus on disk. (a) required_regen_host `convergence_surface_roles` built `seed_embedded_basenames` from `assembled_seed_modules(committed lib.rs mod list, generated_partition_crate_rows() compiled in)` (:7495-:7506) and `convergence_plan_from_model` (:7613) classified each changed surface against that set and built the refusal value at :7744, so a module the change ADDS to a partition crate is absent from the membership set by construction -- the row is what the PR authors -- and its own mirror classified `<basename> has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition`, which is the arm `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_first_unresolved` refuses the whole stage on. (b) `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `lib_rs_module_is_partition_owned` asked the same compiled copy, so the emitted lib.rs declared a mod the partition had just claimed and the next generation deleted it. Both now read one population per round: `emitted_tree_packages` reads the declared rows off the corpus (the route that already exists for the emitted-edge admission, whose own comment states why -- the rows compiled into THIS binary are the predecessor's, #12171's bootstrap deadlock broken on #12185 only by hand-seeding the mirror) and the render receives them as an argument along compile_sources_selected -> emit_resolved_for_target_selected -> emit_from_artifact_plan -> emit_artifact -> emit_rust_selected -> emit_lib_rs_from_paths -> lib_rs_module_is_partition_owned. THE FAMILY IS EIGHT CRATE ROOTS, ALL INSPECTED: the stage0 crate root (90 pub mod lines plus one plain mod compiler_tests, 91 declarations) plus the seven partition roots (stage0_runtime 1, stage0_std_core 55, stage0_std_surface 4, stage0_extdeps_languages 14, stage0_v1_artifact 2, stage0_v1_infer 23, stage0_emit_core 13 pub mod lines -- measured at this head, and the population declares exactly seven GeneratedPartitionCrateRow instances, one per root), one of which (stage0_v1_infer) is entirely #[path into ../../stage0/src re-exports of host-shell modules, the same membership question in a second syntax. Inspected and EXCLUDED, each for a reason: GeneratedFacadeCrate is a declared kind no row uses today, so there is no ninth root; gunbc_stage0_stage0_executable_assembly_generated.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs and emitted_population.rs carry zero pub mod lines (data surfaces, not roots); v1_rt.rs is one generated module whose only mod items are three inline *_tests blocks. The seven partition roots never flipped -- the candidate side already rendered them over the fresh rows, required_regen_host partition_move_explained_by_this_change calling partition_crate_boundary_emit_outcome_over(packages.rows) -- which is why only the stage0 root oscillated. The DIRECTION of that oscillation fixes the fixed point: emit_lib_rs_from_paths (v1.compiler.emit_rust, the has_compiler_tests branch) declares on the MIXED-AUTHORITY host-shell root ONLY the names no partition row owns -- the carrier words it as THE HOST SHELL DECLARES WHAT THE PARTITION DOES NOT OWN, and the subtraction is what makes the duplicate unwritable -- while wholly-generated partition roots subtract nothing. The specimen's module is owned by the v1-stage0-v1-infer row (src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag, stage0_v1_infer_modules; its crate root went 23 to 24 pub mod lines at the specimen's generation-0 install, and generated_host_shell_partition_dependencies is exactly the single package v1-stage0-v1-infer, dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_executable_assembly_generated.dag:11, which is the only package the host shell glob-re-exports), so the host shell has exactly ONE correct rendering of that root: do NOT declare the module, 90 declarations, main's bytes. It is the STALE copy that cannot subtract and so writes the module into the host shell AND into the partition crate -- one file, two compilation stories, the duplicate the carrier comment exists to prevent. The clause this row once read as the defect, lib.rs flips back to main's bytes, is therefore the surface ARRIVING at its fixed point while a predecessor population pulls it toward the duplicate; with one authority for both readers, git status over a run reports lib.rs unchanged. That same seam is where a partition crate root is written (v1_compiler_stage0_crates :915, :1080, :1125, :1206 build the path as spec.crate_dir + /src/lib.rs) and the convergence host projects and installs it itself (--emit-partition-crates at required_regen_host :6445, --emit-partition-crates --write at :6503), so the row's sixth hand-install is not a human step. THE OVERLAP GATE DOES NOT BLOCK THIS DERIVATION EITHER: the seed-build writer's roster (dag/gunbc/seed_build_artifact_emit.dag:47-62) lists Stage0CratePartitionGeneratedDagArtifact, the .dag projection, and has no .rs counterpart -- so heal's round writing src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs is not two writers for one file, and the gate stage0_round_overlap_cause / HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact (dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag:44-70, run after the round and before the writer) stays silent for it. That gate's own rule is that identical bytes are no change, which is what makes it correct that a PR adding a partition row also commits the regenerated .dag projection: that file is the writer's, and matching it byte for byte is the requirement, not staying out of it. SCOPE OF THE RESTORED CAPABILITY, stated narrowly because one of the six is not heal's to take: of the six installs the #14317 specimen listed, heal now derives the transitional lib.rs, the partition file mirror, the second lib.rs and the partition crate lib.rs; the partition row is authored by design and its .dag projection belongs to the seed-build writer above. The module's FIRST mirror stays an authorial install, and correctly so: the host refuses emitted-but-uncommitted surfaces because an author introducing a module and an emitter inventing a surface produce the identical population, and no arm computed from the populations distinguishes them -- admitting the first would be the conflation the other way. So the capability this row claims is four of the six derived with the partition row as the only authored input, plus one mirror that is committed once, under grant, by the author who introduced the module. Readers, classified later by this row's DEFECT 4 (PR #16373), with the reason for each verdict: v1_compiler_stage0_crates stage0_crate_plan_outcome and stage0_crate_boundary_emit_outcome were left compiled-in at the time of this receipt on the reason that the BUILT SEED projecting its own --emit-partition-crates boundary must answer from the seed it was built as; that reason is only half right, and the correction belongs here rather than in a code comment: the boundary outcome WRITES the boundary files, so for it a replacement partition always is in flight, which makes these two FRESH-AUTHORITY readers that no PR has fixed yet. My first pass moved them onto the fold and srv1 proved that illegal -- they sit inside the stage0 self-compile's source closure (cli_run.rs regen_input_sources seeds every .dag under src/v1 and compile_stage0 compiles exactly that set), so an import of the v2-importing authority from here breaks the seed's own compile -- so at this head they read the compiled-in rows again, and the boundary write rendering an authored-only package's src/lib.rs and manifest is the named next PR, routed through the host bridge and inheriting that constraint. This is a reader left unfixed on a stated reason, not a reader declared legitimate. Still compiled-in, with the reason: partition_crate_boundary_host partition_package_names (names packages for a cargo compile scope, an input to a build and not a fixed-point authority; inspected, and it has no caller), and required_regen_host's #[test] an_emit_that_refuses_hands_back_no_files, whose emit carries no partition in flight so the assertion is the all-or-nothing file rule, which no population can change.",
    "DEFECT 1, RUNG EVIDENCE (2026-11-11, srv1, operator-run): RED, heal route -- the heal invocation (`claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope --source-root dag --source-root src/v2`) at PR #16251 head ba126e56719cf973081b48ef9401ce94acbed90a, base mirror 84f93b33ea843fe1a843b6183b05882fc0314403, identity tree:sha1:120b520230d261e99de8f368abef0cf986cd7e57, uncapped, log srv1:/tmp/red16251.log, lib.rs sampler srv1:/tmp/libsamp.out: EXIT=1 after 1h42m (09:07:06Z to 10:48:57Z). Generation 0 completed -- round.built_seed_regen 25 min, elapsed_ms=1542046, first_generation_equal=false, planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176 declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), FAIL generated surface drift = emitted_population.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs, lib.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs; the candidate lib.rs at 09:51:16Z was dcbb5b3ffcee863296a39cf7db1f86c1d83cd46cfabf19bc81d22fb2373f8abd with 91 pub mod lines and v1_compiler_rest_cause_text present; round.install put it on both crate roots (stage0 lib.rs to dcbb5b3f..., and src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs 24034b7e... to b8483dc29208091825d87d79f539979752942f96911be6ad30fcd7e6d634f872, 23 to 24 pub mod, the re-export root gaining the same module); round.rebuild_from_installed 7 min. NO UnresolvedSeedMembership refusal appeared on this route: generation 1 was refused AT ITS BEGIN by the one-resident-generation bound (`generation begin Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=234332160 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5248946176 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472`), and the checkpoint then restored lib.rs to 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164 -- a restore, not an emitted flip. RED, author route, where the flip this defect describes is what the emission itself shows: at the same head `--required-regen` round 1 drifted lib.rs ALONE and its candidate was 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164, byte-identical to the base mirror, dropping `pub mod v1_compiler_rest_cause_text`. The two values are the oscillation; the 90-line one is the rendering the partition declares correct, and the build failure below is the PARTIAL install named in clause (3), not that value; round 2 seed build then failed with one E0432 and four E0433 naming that module in v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs (at :67 and :43062 of the round-0 INSTALLED emit_rust, which is not the committed file at ba126e56 -- the committed mirror carries zero occurrences). GREEN, three clauses, all required by the row. (1) AUTHOR ROUTE, fixed point, at #16310 head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f: the regenerator built from that tree's own hosts, `--required-regen --source-root dag --source-root src/v2`, iterated two rounds (round 1 drifted exactly v1_compiler_compile.rs, rc=1, elapsed_ms=1572855; that file was installed and the regenerator was rebuilt from the installed tree for round 2) and ended zero drift -- first_generation_equal=true, planned=executed=adjudicated=175, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), rc=0 -- with the change set's generated files installed: v1_compiler_compile.rs 2782274f2ac0f075d6b0e3502b74c3a4b2319b8a6a94f0e8971b36cce443af6e (blob e3b72f059523bed109cf8f0cb0375df3a4158f45), the only file that moves at that head, and v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 4dd771251c8bcb0f4316dba42a7c2cc5c2b27f65d9048d4d95d59d983903e8ee (blob ad2c0b6f6e0a11b44c5ec34474fae41c241a27a7), which drifted in NO round because its candidate was byte-identical to the committed copy. compiler_tests.rs and v1_compiler_compiler_tests_rust.rs are not in the changed set at all at that head: both are main's bytes, and the first emission moved NEITHER of them. (2) HEAL ROUTE on a scratch merge of #16251 with #16310 head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f (srv1 unit acc16251, merge 799a08c199c8ecd6ac3667e4a2bdf69fbb122116 = ba126e56 + c16948d3 by --no-ff, tree db867b6037b9e8ed5aaa572a04ae96c2b42c3cbe, HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT 4b67f390b0225e5f0d5868f83fdcaf33605dca4f, identity tree:sha1:db867b6037b9e8ed5aaa572a04ae96c2b42c3cbe, MemoryMax 64G swap 0, --regen-affected-scope kept, target/stage0-regen-candidate REMOVED and verified absent at 13:47:11Z so no candidate byte can be inherited -- every one of the 255 candidate files at the end carried mtime 14:40, written by this run). Invocation 13:55:29Z-15:42:37Z, EXIT=1, and the exit is attributable entirely to the separately named condition below. Round 1: base mirror paths=302, paths_rewritten=4, head_added_paths_kept=1, head_deleted_paths=0. GENERATION 0, the arm this row names: UnresolvedSeedMembership and 'has no owner in generated_stage0_crate_partition' occurrences across the WHOLE invocation = 0. REPORTED AS A NEGATIVE CONTROL, NOT AS THIS FIX'S EFFECT: the RED specimen on this route printed neither string either (its exit was the resident-generation bound), and in BOTH acc16251 and red16251 the generation-0 image is the base mirror's host -- acc16251 logs 4 journalled paths rewritten to 4b67f390 bytes and its exe_mtime switches to the seed_build image at the generation-0 admission -- so this zero says the heal route does not fire that arm, and the fixed host's own render on the heal route is the separate receipt below titled POST-LANDING SIMULATION, where paths_rewritten=0 and the generation-0 image carries this change. round.built_seed_regen 26 min: elapsed_ms=1588592, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs); the drift set was EXACTLY the four membership surfaces -- emitted_population.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs, lib.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs -- and NOT v1_compiler_compile.rs (the mirror this PR installs, blob e3b72f05..., held against the base-mirror seed) and NOT compiler_tests.rs. round.install wrote them back together with the partition crate root: from the sampler at mtime 15:34:54Z, src/v1/stage0/src/lib.rs became dcbb5b3ffcee... at 91 pub mod lines WITH the module declared, and src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs became b8483dc29208... at 24 pub mod lines with the module declared -- the same bytes runB4 produced and the same bytes the specimen's round.install produced -- and round.rebuild_from_installed then COMPILED that tree. Read this plainly rather than favourably: generation 0 is the PREDECESSOR'S render, because round.built_seed_regen builds its seed crate from the base mirror (302 paths, required_regen_host.rs among them), so both roots declaring one module is what a host shell without the render-side fix emits, and it is the duplicate the carrier comment forbids -- it is not what this row calls converged. GENERATION 1 NEVER RAN, and that is the separately named condition, not this defect: 'required-regen: generation 1 begins; orchestrator resident=5248507904 (at generation 0: 236228608)' then 'regen-round-cost: refused: next generation refused; checkpoint restored: generation begin Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=236228608 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5248507904 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472' (parent.generation_begin_admission ordinal=1 memory.current=6715666432, peak 22248300544). It is the one-resident-generation orchestrator bound, carried as a sighting on gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_resident_cost_taken_before_the_baseline_of_its_own_growth_check, and it refused the specimen at the same ordinal with the same shape. The checkpoint restore at 15:42:23Z returned src/v1/stage0/src/lib.rs to 6605bb7945fa... at 90 and the infer root to 24034b7e... at 23, after which git status --porcelain and git diff --stat were EMPTY -- an EMPTY tree there is the RESTORE, not a fixed point, and this row does not count it as one. The fixed point with the fix in force is measured by clause (3) instead, where the regenerator IS the installed tree. No generated file was hand-installed beyond the module's own first mirror, which cool-tern-790 committed under grants msg_23e9c13d and msg_0586b869, and there was no push to #16251. (3) AUTHOR ROUTE OVER THE MERGED TREE, the control that separates the two readers (srv1 unit greenb-16251, merge 729b781f923871cdffcb9bf5545474454629986f, tree 85a7c72fa749e544f13bc158a09a68addd51a87b, base mirror 4b67f390b0225e5f0d5868f83fdcaf33605dca4f, regenerator built from the merged tree's own hosts, generation 0 elapsed_ms=1580216, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), SeedMembership count 0): the emission MOVED THE PARTITION and the renderer together -- emitted_population.rs 78db2eb1... to 423b93bc... (the source line for the module added), gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs 8e5d6966... to 41586473... (the v1-stage0-v1-infer row's modules vector gaining it, 23 to 24) and v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 4dd77125... to 47d4a92e... (references to it 0 to 2) -- while lib.rs was NOT in the drift set: its fresh candidate, written 12:57:27Z, was 6605bb7945fa6d1a67c4c7b2ca2659c2f6fe1e99fc6a13beff25f864b0f3f164 with 90 pub mod lines and the module ABSENT, the partition-owned rendering this row now names as the fixed point. THE FOURTH SURFACE IS OWNED BY A DECLARED ROUTE, AND MEASUREMENT SEPARATES IT FROM A HAND-INSTALL: `claim_executor --emit-partition-crates` renders from the COMPILED-IN rows on purpose -- partition_crate_boundary_host.rs, run_partition_crate_boundary doc comment: 'On a round that moves the partition the compiled-in rows are the predecessor's, so the regen round renders from the candidate tree's rows (partition_crate_boundary_emit_outcome_over) and hands the outcome here' -- and heal's install uses the RENDERED-POPULATION entry, required_regen_host.rs:6574-6575 taking rows from emitted_tree_packages(workspace) and :7102 writing them with run_partition_crate_boundary_over(write=true). Measured pair on srv1 (unit runB4-16251): with the partition mirror, emitted_population.rs and v1_compiler_compile.rs installed and the binary rebuilt from that tree, --emit-partition-crates --write took src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs 24034b7e with 23 pub mod lines to b8483dc2 with 24, the same bytes heal's own install route wrote in the specimen's round.install and installing the candidate emit_rust then built clean, BUILD_B_RC=0; the same CLI on the PRE-FIX binary reported rendered=14 written=0 and the build kept exactly one E0432 at v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs:67 and four E0433 inside :43351, all naming v1_compiler_rest_cause_text in the crate root -- the identical five errors cool-tern-790 met at round 2, which is why this row calls that round a PARTIAL install of three of the six rather than a codegen defect. THE FIXED POINT ITSELF, MEASURED (srv1 unit runB5, staged control, not the acceptance run): with those five surfaces installed -- emitted_population.rs 423b93bc, the partition mirror 41586473, v1_compiler_compile.rs blob e3b72f05, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 47d4a92e, src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs b8483dc2 at 24 pub mod -- over the merged tree, and the regenerator being the build of exactly that tree, `--required-regen` returned rc=0, elapsed_ms=1426979, first_generation_equal=true, planned=executed=adjudicated=176, declared_divergent=1 (main.rs), candidate-vs-tree diff list EMPTY, all 255 candidate files written by that run (13:55Z), target/stage0-regen-candidate removed beforehand at 13:40:10Z. The candidate host-shell lib.rs was 6605bb7945fa... at 90 pub mod lines with the module NOT declared, and a read-only `--emit-partition-crates` with the same binary reported rendered=14 written=0 divergent=[] -- so the infer crate root is at its own fixed point too. NO SIXTH SURFACE APPEARED. That is the statement this row needed: with the partition row authored, the six surfaces that used to be hand-installed form a closed set that the regenerator reproduces byte for byte, and the stage0 host shell settles WITHOUT declaring the module. CI on the PR: at head c16948d3124c454f5164b3f280f74b7bfe14e54f both lanes are SUCCESS -- v2-bootstrap (job 130560719439, whose step 28 'Typecheck the v1 unit-test population' was the single E0061 that the superseded mirror state produced) and heal-generated-artifacts (job 130560877728, which passed step 7 'Converge the stage0 mirrors to the seed's own fixed point' and the step 8 overlap gate). This ledger row is a .dag text edit only: it adds no carrier and no host, so it moves no generated surface, and the lanes re-run at the head that carries it.",
    "DEFECT 1, POST-LANDING SIMULATION -- THE ONE HEAL ROUTE ON WHICH THE FIXED HOST DECIDES MEMBERSHIP (2026-11-11, srv1 unit pl16251, operator-run, scratch, unpushed, no push to #16251): head 427fea854b8fca6e3be457fe172ab774353334ab = the scratch merge 799a08c199c8ecd6ac3667e4a2bdf69fbb122116 of #16251 with #16310 head c16948d3, plus jolly-newt-497's two #16318 commits 706467466248 and 2002d1ba0b5b, that PR's tip as measured here -- #16318 may gain commits, so every refusal below is a verdict on this tip only; tree bdfb58c9ffbd4395c3441cd1ff105bdbcd270bc5; HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT 3203ac1dd219fc12942f2f843975e1c76287c0bc = that same #16310 head plus those two picks. That is the state a seed-module PR meets once this row's fix is on main: the base mirror already carries it, so the stage0-crate delta base''..head is the single added module mirror and the whole-tree delta is #16251's own ten files. Precondition checked before the run: required_regen_host.rs, cli_run/emit_host.rs, v1_compiler_compile.rs and v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs are byte-identical between base'' and head. Binary sha 1a15a1d89452235b built 17:28:54Z; invocation 17:28:55Z-18:49:57Z, EXIT=1, MemoryMax 64G swap 0, --regen-affected-scope, stop guard never fired, target/stage0-regen-candidate removed at 17:21:05Z. Round 1 logs paths=302 paths_rewritten=0 head_added_paths_kept=1 head_deleted_paths=0 and base_snapshot_revert '0 journalled paths were rewritten' -- nothing of mine was reverted, which is the difference from the two runs above. Provenance of the image that decided membership: exe_mtime is 17:28:54Z (the build of head) through line 54 and 17:54:59Z -- the image round.seed_build wrote -- from line 60, the first post-exec model_resolve, through the generation-0 admission at line 79 and the generation-0 child at line 124, the seed_build image built from base'' which holds my hosts unchanged, and jolly-newt-497's #16318 model_resolve phases fire after that exec, which they did not in the run where the host was reverted. GENERATION 0, the measurement this row exists for: admission ordinal=0 orchestrator_resident=235876352; round.built_seed_regen elapsed_ms=1531661 first_generation_equal=false planned=executed=adjudicated=176 declared_divergent=1 [main.rs]; FAIL drift is THREE files -- emitted_population.rs, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs -- and lib.rs is NOT among them: the candidate lib.rs (mtime 18:12:02Z, with all 255 candidate files written at 18:12 by this run) is 6605bb7945fa, 90 pub mod lines, v1_compiler_rest_cause_text NOT declared, equal to the tree. That is the symptom this row records, gone: on the same route the predecessor host drifted lib.rs and emitted it declaring the module (acc16251 and red16251, candidate dcbb5b3ffcee, 91 pub mod), while the fixed host leaves the crate root untouched. round.install, 21 min including a 6 min rebuild_from_installed, wrote at 18:42:47Z: src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs 24034b7e at 23 pub mod to b8483dc29208 at 24 with the module DECLARED, the partition mirror 8e5d6966 to 41586473c33d, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs 4dd77125 to 47d4a92ef99a; the host shell lib.rs was NOT rewritten and stays 6605bb at 90 with no declaration, and emitted_population.rs drifted but showed no mtime change at install, so its installation is UNOBSERVED rather than claimed. The three installed values are byte-identical to the closed author-route state of unit runB5, and rebuild_from_installed compiled them: the module is declared ONCE, by the inferred partition root, reached through the host shell's re-export -- one compilation story. SeedMembership and has-no-owner occurrences, whole invocation: 0. GENERATION 1 never ran, and this is NOT a fixed point: the checkpoint restored the three installed files at 18:49:37Z and the tree is clean, which is a restore. The named condition is jolly-newt-497's bound, not this row's defect -- generation 1 begins orchestrator resident=5253963776 against 235876352 at generation 0, then Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=235876352 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5253963776 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472, attributed to one parent model_resolve of dag/gunbc/regen_round_cost.dag modules=748 taking VmRSS 233748kB to 5129916kB and retained to the admission, the same shape as unit jt2-16251. So a zero-drift generation built from an installed tree is still unproven ON THE HEAL ROUTE; the closest measured evidence for it is unit runB5 on the author route over the same five-file state, which returned zero drift. Logs srv1 /tmp/pl16251.log, /tmp/pl.out, /tmp/pl-libsamp.out; worktrees pl-16251 and plbase-16251 kept and locked.",
    "DEFECT 2, READ AS ALREADY FIXED (aa761c29cfe3, #14340, 2026-10-18, the day after this row was filed): the receipt above (a 2026-10-16 run) predates it. `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_stage_plan_kind_label` (src/v2/workflow/regen_convergence_transaction.dag:657) now renders the refused arm (:754, same shape at :184, :777, :1176, :1183) as `Refused: ` ++ `regen_convergence_refusal_detail(refusal)`, which spells variant, surface identity (declaring module + projected path) and reason. The host reads that label at src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs:7943-7951; a refused label matches none of the three closed stage-kind strings, so the host returns `refusal: convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant` with the rendered label interpolated at :7962-7965, which is how the payload reaches the operator; pinned by the control test `a_stage_planning_refusal_prints_its_variant_surface_and_reason` in src/v2/test/claim/regen_convergence_transaction_witness.dag, which asserts the label contains the reason string. Execution showing the renderer: run by quick-newt-573 on main 9bc7a3ebcadd8d4f9e0348ec8d386ffdf9937031 (contains aa761c29) as claim_batch --hermetic --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/regen_convergence_transaction_witness.dag --functions a_stage_planning_refusal_prints_its_variant_surface_and_reason, which printed PASS with exit 0 (binary sha256 01a98d7d56607bbceee7807d39c12296548bc40d5fe249892cc10c9ec8ad9715, file blob 7303b33a); its scope is the renderer over a fixture plan, not the host call. Execution showing the host path: srv1 run red16251 at ba126e56 printed a host-rendered refusal carrying its whole payload, `generation begin Refused: GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator ordinal=1 orchestrator_resident_bytes_at_first_generation=234332160 orchestrator_resident_bytes_now=5248946176 growth_bound_bytes=3221225472` (srv1:/tmp/red16251.log).",
    "NEXT RUNG, DEFECT 1's SUCCESSOR, RECORDED NOT BUILT (2026-11-11, eager-gull-72, at #16310; the first two triggers in the NEXT-RUNG receipt above are now met for the membership arm by the two commits of #16310). CURRENT DELIBERATE STANDING: the missing-mirror arm refuses EVERY emitted-but-uncommitted surface (the emitted_not_committed arm of validate_compared_populations in required_regen_host.rs), so a new seed module costs one operator grant to install its first mirror -- the host's own comment at :484-490 concedes the case is the normal one, that adding a module to the v1 seed closure produces emitted_not_committed BY CONSTRUCTION on that module's first commit, and that the candidate tree is the author's only route to the file they are told to commit. TRIGGER FOR THE NEXT RUNG: the missing-mirror arm admits a surface whose module carries a declared partition row in the change's own FRESH corpus (v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition, read the way #16310 now reads the partition) and keeps refusing one with no row -- which is distinguishable evidence the check was never given, the population alone cannot separate authored from invented but a declared row can. WHY THE ROW ALONE IS NOT A SUFFICIENT DISCRIMINATOR, as asked: (a) a mirror fabricated for a module that legitimately HAS a row is admitted by that gate, and fabricating a surface for an existing module is exactly the regression the check exists to catch; (b) there is no declared derivation from a module name to its mirror basename anywhere in the corpus, so nothing can test whether an invented basename is the one that module should have -- the only declared path rule is path_is_stage0_mirror (dag/gunbc/heal_publication_boundary.dag:539-550), which admits by SHAPE, a .rs directly under src/v1/stage0/src, and a fabricated name satisfies shape as easily as a legitimate one. SUFFICIENT FORM needs both: the fresh partition row, AND a declared one-mirror-per-declared-module naming rule so an invented basename has no derivation and still refuses. Until then the price of not deciding is one grant per new seed module, and this row keeps the standing refusal as the deliberate current state.",
    "CORRECTION TO THE NEXT-RUNG CLAUSE, WITHDRAWN AND REPLACED (2026-11-11, eager-gull-72, at #16358): clause (b) of the NEXT-RUNG receipt above asserted there is NO declared derivation from a module name to its mirror basename anywhere in the corpus, and offered `path_is_stage0_mirror` as the only declared path rule. That assertion is FALSE and is withdrawn. The derivation exists, is declared, and is what the emitter itself uses: `gunbc.rust_emitted_edge::module_to_filename` (dag/gunbc/rust_emitted_edge.dag:55) joins a `.`-separated module path with `_`, and `gunbc.rust_emitted_edge::rust_module_emit_filename` (:59) applies it with the one collision the carrier names, module `main` spelling `main_mod`; the host mirror is src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_rust_emitted_edge.rs:50 and :60. What `path_is_stage0_mirror` is (dag/gunbc/heal_publication_boundary.dag:543, not the :539 the clause cited) is the PUBLISHER'S path policy -- a `.rs` directly under src/v1/stage0/src, admitted by shape so a change's own regeneration may be written -- and it was never a naming rule, so it was not the sibling the clause was looking for. THE GAP WAS THEREFORE NOT A MISSING AUTHORITY BUT AN UNCONSULTED ONE, which changes the shape of the fix: the admission was asking two populations a question the corpus had already answered, and the repair is one call to the declared fn (`declared_mirror_basename`, src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs:1770) rather than a new rule invented beside it. That the distinction is not cosmetic is shown by what the clause got right: a row alone is still not a sufficient discriminator, because a fabricated mirror for a module that legitimately has a row would be admitted by the row alone, so the gate that closes it is the projection, and the two-population control `witness_new_surface_alone_still_refuses` still PASSes with the admission in place.",
    "NEXT RUNG REALIZED, PART 1 -- THE DECISION AND ITS CLAIMS (2026-11-11, eager-gull-72, PR #16358): the discriminant the carrier's own note said was missing is now modeled -- `MissingMirrorAuthority` (src/v2/workflow/required_regen.dag:250), `MissingMirrorAdmission` (:254), `missing_mirror_admission` (:325), and the `AdmittedAuthorIntroducedMirror` outcome arm (:75), added to every collector that enumerates the outcome type so a fold cannot silently drop it -- and realized in the host (src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs:1701-1855), DECLARED as the second copy it is by dag/gunbc/missing_mirror_admission_seed_growth.dag and pinned on the running side by two sync witnesses in the claim lane, with the four rules that keep it from being a rubber stamp: absence of an authority admits NOTHING and there is no fallback to the rows compiled into the running binary, which are the predecessor's and cannot contain the module being introduced (that fallback would re-open DEFECT 1 in a new place); shape never admits -- the name must be the projection of a declared module through the emitter's own file rule `gunbc.rust_emitted_edge::rust_module_emit_filename` (src/v1/stage0/src/gunbc_rust_emitted_edge.rs:60) and nothing else, so a module projecting to `main` owns `main_mod.rs`, because that is the file the emitter writes for it: v1.compiler.emit_rust `rust_module_emit_path` builds a module's emitted path from that same function and the compared population is denominated by that path, so a `main.rs` is a name nothing produces and refuses like any invented basename. THIS SENTENCE HAS BEEN WRONG TWICE in this row and both states are left here rather than overwritten. It first read that the entry-file rule applied; a reviewer-facing revision then reversed it to the pure projection `module_to_filename`, on the argument that a stage0 mirror is never the crate's entry file since the root is lib.rs, and called the emitter's rule a bug that would admit a name no emitter writes. That reversal was the error, and it did not survive execution: the witness fleet came back 21 PASS and 1 FAIL, the failure being `witness_an_undeclared_basename_refuses_however_plausible_its_shape`, which had been right throughout and was reddened by my edit rather than by any change in the subject. The rule is now pinned by `witness_a_module_projecting_to_main_owns_the_name_the_emitter_writes` on the model side and `witness_the_host_asks_the_emitter_s_file_rule_and_never_a_hand_rolled_join` plus the host spelling test on the running side. Exposure on today's corpus is zero either way - every declared unit name is flat and none is `main` - which is exactly why this needed an executed reading of the fleet and not a reading of the carrier; an ambiguous projection REFUSES and names every module it is refusing between, because `a.b_c` and `a.b.c` spell one basename and a first-match search would admit whichever row came first, deciding an admission by row ORDER; and a hand-maintained shadow is not admittable by any declaration, because both remedies of the missing-mirror class destroy hand-authored code. ESTABLISHED BY EXECUTION: `claim_batch --hermetic --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/required_regen_admission_witness.dag` gives 18/18 PASS at rc=0 in 237 s, and the same entry over main's copies gives 13/13 PASS at rc=0 in 239 s -- the 13 pre-existing witnesses PASS unchanged on my copies and none is inherited broken (quick-newt-573, msg_d40f7313, scratch tree at main 34143ec0, claim_batch sha256 f5cc740e). STANDING OF THAT READING, stated so it is not over-read: it exercised the two carriers as they stood BEFORE the projection correction at af80c93999ba -- 18 witnesses, four of which (the entry-file discriminator, the partition flatness reading, and the two host sync witnesses) did not exist yet -- so it establishes the model leg on a superseded revision, and the same entry at the tip is requested and not returned. The host legs are NOT established and no reading is claimed for them: the first `cargo check -p v1-compiler --all-targets` over the host change came back RED (quick-newt-573, msg_5a60c711 -- `Deserialize` not in scope at required_regen_host.rs:1149, `AdmittedMissingMirror` lacking `PartialEq`/`Debug` for the join comparison at :649 and the asserts at :3751/:3859); the fix is committed and the re-run is requested, not returned, so the 7 new host unit tests have never been executed -- a different standing from a witnessed claim, which is why they are not cited as evidence. ESTABLISHED SINCE THE DRAFT ABOVE: `cargo check -p v1-compiler --all-targets` at af80c93999ba is rc=0 with 0 warnings and 0 errors (quick-newt-573, msg_8438cc66), on the host file at sha256 16ee26c32dc7547d458075da727f7c407b3f5ca6f8cb7217ab3dd5dce84e7af2, which is the file at this head -- the four lib and ten lib-test errors of msg_5a60c711 are gone. `cargo test -p v1-compiler` is still requested and not returned, so the new unit tests remain unexecuted. NOT YET ESTABLISHED, and the rung does not move without it: that heal on the merge path ADMITS the probe module's missing first mirror, INSTALLS it as AbsentBeforeInstall beside the membership surfaces, and reaches a generation with nothing left to restage -- the srv1 run -- together with CI at the head. A note on this ledger's own integrity: an earlier draft of this receipt attributed a clean `cargo check` and a `cargo test` reading of 548 passed / 0 failed to quick-newt-573 under message id msg_5d10f820, which quick-newt-573 denies sending and which does not exist in this session's transcript. It is WITHDRAWN and nothing here rests on it (2026-11-11). The rule it broke is the one this row exists to enforce: no clause and no rung moves on a reading nobody produced. HOST LEGS NOW EXECUTED (2026-11-12, after the fix to the RED below): `cargo check -p v1-compiler --all-targets` rc=0 with 0 warnings and 0 errors, and the filtered run of the seven `#[test]` fns this change adds, `-- --test-threads=1`, returned verbatim `test result: ok. 7 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1183 filtered out` at head 593f27442ea7 on host sha256 649bef56 (quick-newt-573, msg_b3ae909c, local arm64). An earlier draft of this receipt said eight such tests; quick-newt-573 counted seven and is right, the eighth name I carried is the `test_authority` helper, and the count is corrected rather than quietly amended. SEPARATE SIGHTING, pre-existing and not filed by me: `cli_run::demanded_typecheck_equivalence::a_read_outside_the_realized_set_refuses_typed` spins at 100% CPU with no result both on this branch (35 min, killed) and at 34143ec0 itself (10-minute cap, rc=124) per quick-newt-573 msg_7a4357f0, so the whole-crate `cargo test` total remains unreturned and is NOT claimed anywhere here.",
    "DEFECT 1, ONE-INVOCATION CONVERGENCE ON THE LIVE SPECIMEN (2026-11-12, srv1, bold-wren-111 msg_b0fc7207, run ppx-16358, scratch, unpushed, no push to #16251): merging #16251 (ba126e56719cf973081b48ef9401ce94acbed90a) --no-ff onto this branch at 6da40894 over base 9551388b (= 82de3d65 + 6da40894) gives head 2f671dcd, whose stage0 diff against that base is `A src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs` alone -- the one file its author committed under a grant -- and every other generated surface is left to heal. ONE heal invocation converged: EXIT=0, REGEN_START 00:32:34Z, REGEN_END 02:10:46Z, receipt `wall_ms=5799456`, `convergence_stages=2`, `WholeCompilerRebuildRequired` with `rebuild_packages=2` listing v1-compiler and v1-stage0-v1-infer. Ordinal 0 drifted `emitted_population.rs`, `gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs` and `v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs`, and the install wrote them plus the module list `src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs` (`24034b7e` to `b8483dc2`, 24 pub mods, now declaring `v1_compiler_rest_cause_text`); ordinal 1 was ADMITTED and drifted `emitted_population.rs` alone (installed as `423b93bc`); ordinal 2 was ADMITTED and drifted NOTHING, verbatim: `required-regen: elapsed_ms=1023416 first_generation_equal=true planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176 declared_divergent=1 [main.rs]`. `UnresolvedSeedMembership` and the string `has no owner` appear zero times over the whole invocation, and neither `GenerationStateRetainedByOrchestrator` nor `Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered` fired. The receipt carries `admitted_new_surfaces` as the empty list and the admission line never printed, which is the correct reading of THIS specimen rather than a silence to explain: #16251 commits its own mirror, so nothing was missing from the tree, and what the admission is for here is keeping heal's own derived surfaces installable. WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES: the six hand-installs this row listed per new module are down to the single mirror the author commits, on a real PR, in one invocation. THE RUNG STAYS WHERE IT IS (manager instruction, and on the evidence): the same recipe with the committed generated surfaces deleted (ppy-16358, msg_954b1241) still refuses in the seed rebuild at `Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered` on five endpoints, so the crate-root family is not closed while that stands. CONFIRMED ON THE LANDING TIP OWN CODE, NOT INFERRED: ppz-16358 (msg_1eb5f7e7; base b0a82a44 = 82de3d65 + 593f27442ea7, head 8d0ec8dd) reached EXIT=0, REGEN_START 01:05:06Z, REGEN_END 02:42:18Z, `wall_ms=5659969`, with the identical drift list in every generation, an empty diff over the sampler (path, sha) sequence, byte-identical final four files (`b8483dc2`, `41586473`, `47d4a92e`, `423b93bc`), zero refusals and zero `has no owner`, differing from ppx only in `executable_digest` -- which the host change requires",
    "DEFECT 4, THE AUTHORITY MOVED FOR THE READERS THAT CAN REACH IT, AND A CONSTRAINT EXECUTION TAUGHT (2026-11-12, eager-gull-72, PR #16373; srv1 receipts bold-wren-111 msg_954b1241 and msg_0ccf52cc). RED, executed: the strict variant of #16251 (only the partition row authored, the mirror and the carrier row absent, nothing hand-installed) refused in generation 0 -- required-regen: refused: Stage0EmittedEdgesNotCovered: 5 emitted edge endpoint(s) have no stage0 crate (neither a module-bearing partition row nor the host shell lists them), naming v1_compiler_rest_cause_text, EXIT=1, paths=303 paths_rewritten=0, nothing installed. CAUSE: the emitted-edge admission's package graph was assembled by the host from the carrier's committed data, and the carrier is a snapshot refreshed by claim_executor --emit-partition-crates --write in the install step of the run that has already refused, so a row this change authored could not be seen. THE ARM NOW FIRES, executed: the same construction, with the admission asking the fold instead, resolved and passed -- model_resolve entry=.../dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_emitted_edge_admission.dag modules=34 items=1198, then decode.shell and decode.end, SeedMembership and has-no-owner occurrences 0. WHAT CHANGED: one authored-to-generated mapping, gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_emit::generated_partition_crate_row_from_authority over v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition::stage0_partition_crate_rows, with gunbc.stage0.stage0_partition_rebuild_scope and gunbc.repo.repo_self_build reading the fold through it (both are outside the seed's self-compile closure) and the host resolving gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_emit over the corpus roots that cli_run::witness_layer_roots declares, rather than decoding the carrier. THE CONSTRAINT, found by execution and not by review: the stage0 self-compile compiles exactly the sources of the population it is emitting -- cli_run.rs regen_input_sources seeds every .dag under src/v1 and grows the closure through import edges over src/v1 and dag, and required_regen_host.rs compile_stage0 compiles that set -- so NO module reachable by import from an src/v1 seed may import a v2-authored module. The first attempt at this fix put the fold where an src/v1 seed would import it and srv1 died with seven hard diagnostics, all rooted in one import: unresolved import: module 'v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition' not found (imported by 'gunbc.stage0.stage0_crate_partition_emit'). That is why the carrier is literal data, and it is why the fold lives in the carrier's own renderer and stays outside that closure. Guarded by dag/test/claim/required_regen_admission_witness.dag::the_seed_corpus_never_imports_the_declared_partition_authority, which goes red on any src/v1 import of the fold's module and on a second declaration of it. WHAT THIS PR DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: src/v1/stage0_crates.dag (the partition crate plan and the boundary write) is INSIDE that closure, so it keeps its compiled-in rows, with the reason on this row -- the built seed projecting itself. The boundary write rendering an authored-only package's src/lib.rs and manifest is the next PR, and it inherits this constraint; it is the half that produced the E0432/E0433 when #16251's candidate was compiled. The host-side witness for the machinery it will need is already in place: the_boundary_write_gives_an_authored_only_package_its_manifest_and_module_list in src/v1/stage0/src/required_regen_host.rs.",
    "DEFECT 4, THE ADMISSION ARM FIRES ON A STRICT SPECIMEN AND THE ROUND THEN DIES AT THE BOUNDARY (2026-11-12, PR #16373 head e44fdfc4b5c4a215324e1ab73266107d1e18eee8, srv1 unit ppe-16373, bold-wren-111 msg_7812c8da; base c3287d99 = 6ad855dc9a33 + e44fdfc4, headX 553b0259 = base + ba126e56, strict head 5e302d4e tree 765f2353 with src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs DELETED and the carrier .dag row REMOVED, so the authored partition row is the only thing the change carries; HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT=c3287d99, --regen-affected-scope, 64G, swap 0, 9-name drift guard). PASSED, in the order the run printed them. Self-compile: no 'v2 self-compile produced N hard diagnostic(s)' anywhere -- the closure constraint holds at this head, which is what b23289ada3cc bought. Emitted-edge admission, verbatim: required-regen: emitted-edge admission admitted edges=2557. THE ARM THIS PR EXISTS FOR, verbatim: required-regen: admitted 1 author-introduced mirror(s) declared by this change's partition: v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs <- v1_compiler_rest_cause_text, and the receipt carries admitted_new_surfaces as [{\"basename\": \"v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs\", \"declared_module\": \"v1_compiler_rest_cause_text\"}] -- NON-EMPTY, where ppx-16358 and ppz-16358 both printed it empty because their specimens committed their own mirror. Generation 0, verbatim: required-regen: elapsed_ms=1084373 first_generation_equal=false planned=175 executed=176 adjudicated=175 declared_divergent=1 [main.rs], drifting emitted_population.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs and v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs -- the mirror heal was refusing to write before, now written (55adbe11, byte-identical to #16251's committed mirror, so the emitter and the author agree). SeedMembership and has-no-owner: 0 occurrences. paths_rewritten=0, ordinal=0 orchestrator_resident=235859968, and the emitted_tree resolve ran twice in the generation-0 child at +2.4 MB and +103 MB -- small class, as predicted. THEN IT DIED ONE STEP ON, exactly where this row's DEFECT 4 says the remaining gap is: regen-round-cost: refused: stage seed build refused; checkpoint restored: refusal: cargo build (round.rebuild_from_installed) failed with exit status: 101 -- error[E0432]: unresolved import crate::v1_compiler_rest_cause_text --> src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs:67:16, and E0433 at :43351. THE MECHANISM OF THE DEATH, from the run's own lines: phase=parent.round.drifted.stage_scope_decided whole_compiler=false boundary=0, and src/v1/stage0_v1_infer/src/lib.rs stayed 24034b7ea76c (23 pub mods) for the WHOLE run -- nothing writes the partition crate root for an author-introduced module, so the emit_rust that names it cannot compile. Same shape as the E0432 in the author-route loop when --emit-partition-crates was skipped. WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES, and what it does not: the six hand-installs this row listed per new module are down to ZERO for every surface the seed derives -- mirror, emitted_population, emit_rust, the carrier .rs -- on a strict specimen that authors nothing but the partition row; the capability restored by DEFECT 1 and DEFECT 4 does not yet include the crate-root write, so the strict specimen does NOT converge and the rung STAYS. TWO THINGS A LATER AUTHOR MUST NOT MISS. First, planned=175 against executed=176: the admitted surface was executed without being planned, so the convergence plan does not yet know about an admitted surface -- the same blind spot as boundary=0, seen from the planner side. Second, the two readers this PR leaves compiled-in (src/v1/stage0_crates.dag stage0_crate_plan_outcome and stage0_crate_boundary_emit_outcome) are the ones that would have to answer it, and they cannot import the declared authority because they sit inside the seed's self-compile closure: the next PR must route the rows through the host bridge, and this row's closure paragraph is its constraint. ppe-16373 is the specimen to re-run when it does: same recipe, same 9-name guard, bar EXIT=0 with the infer root gaining pub mod v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.",
    "DEFECT 4, ONE HEAL INVOCATION, NOTHING HAND-INSTALLED -- THE STRICT SPECIMEN CONVERGES (2026-11-12, PR #16377 head 8607ea54de970a876a7b1d0345d5c461a37294cf, srv1 unit ppf-16377, bold-wren-111 msg_cf50a775; the run measured c8a86e86304f and git diff c8a86e86304f..8607ea54de97 over the two Rust files has ZERO non-comment changed lines, so what was measured is what the head does). SPECIMEN: base = 90788b78 = (main d700a0f81824 + git revert of 2bcad60f, the landed specimen PR) --no-ff the head; head = 93da6320 (tree a2aeac3f) = that base + the change's 8 AUTHORED files only; the diff base..head is EXACTLY those 8 files, with nothing under src/v1/stage0 and nothing in the carrier .dag. Pre-state read before the run: 3 authored files, 0 rows in the carrier .dag and 0 in its .rs mirror, the mirror absent from src/v1/stage0/src, stage0 lib.rs 6605bb7945fa with 90 pub mods, the partition crate root 24034b7ea76c with 23 pub mods, HEAL_BASE_MIRROR_COMMIT at the base, a 9-name drift guard, nothing installed by hand. RESULT EXIT=0, wall_ms=5079646. THE MISSING-MIRROR ADMISSION FIRED: required-regen admitted 1 author-introduced mirror declared by this change's partition, v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs <- v1_compiler_rest_cause_text, and heal WROTE that first mirror itself (09:38:26Z, sha 55adbe11071a, byte-identical to the landed blob). THE BOUNDARY MOVED IN GENERATION 0, verbatim phase=parent.round.drifted.stage_scope_decided whole_compiler=true boundary=1 partition_moved=false -- the same line the previous head (unit ppe-16373, head e44fdfc4b5c4) read as whole_compiler=false boundary=0 before dying at round.rebuild_from_installed with E0432 -- followed by partition-rebuild: selected whole-compiler build; boundary_files_changed=true; PartitionRebuildScopeDerived changed_mirrors=[v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs, v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs] owning_packages=[v1-compiler, v1-stage0-v1-infer]. The partition crate root moved inside round.install and BEFORE the stage build: 24034b7ea76c with 23 pub mods at 08:51:14Z to b8483dc29208 with 24 at 09:38:25Z, and the final diff of that root is exactly three added lines: #[rustfmt::skip], the #[path] attribute naming ../../stage0/src/v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs, and pub mod v1_compiler_rest_cause_text;. THE STAGE BUILD THEN SUCCEEDED: round.rebuild_from_installed done in 7 minutes (wall_ms=458819, whole compiler), where the previous head died after 41 seconds. GENERATIONS: gen0 first_generation_equal=false planned=175 executed=176 adjudicated=175 declared_divergent=1 [main.rs] drifting emitted_population.rs, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs, v1_compiler_rest_cause_text.rs; gen1 first_generation_equal=false planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176 drifting only emitted_population.rs; gen2 first_generation_equal=true planned=176 executed=176 adjudicated=176 with NO drift named. planned==executed from gen 1 onward, including the converging generation, so the admission closed the 175/176 gap gen 0 still showed. The guard never fired; BoundaryDriftRefused, CheckpointJournalWithoutRoundSubject and PartitionProjectionUnobserved each appear 0 times; the end-of-run emitted-partition-crates dry check read rendered=14 written=0 mode=read-only divergent=[]. THE FOUR FILES THE RUN LEFT IN THE TREE ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL TO THE LANDED BLOBS: emitted_population.rs a1b20530, v1_compiler_emit_rust.rs a6626e3b, the partition crate root 995210e4, and the new mirror 58451296. WHAT FIXED IT, in the host: ONE fn boundary_outcome_from_declared_partition in required_regen_host.rs now renders the crate-root family (the boundary query that built_seed_boundary_drift asks AND the writer run_partition_crate_boundary in partition_crate_boundary_host.rs), where the query had folded the candidate rows but the writer rendered the compiled-in snapshot; the boundary query is no longer gated on partition_moved, which is written only AFTER the install and the stage build, so generation 0 could never ask it; and establish_round_subject now runs before install_built_seed_boundary, which journals under that subject. COST OF THE UNCONDITIONAL QUERY, the reading the acceptance was made subject to: small class. The cgroup moved 1,865,854,976 to 1,872,171,008 bytes (+6.3 MB) across the whole boundary decision, the orchestrator step of +233 MB coincides with the decider model load which the previous head also paid (+238 MB) so no separate cost is attributable to the model resolve the bridge added, and the tail from the generation child exit to the root write is under 20 seconds at 5-second granularity with the cgroup between 1.83 and 2.03 GB; generation peaks stayed 6.5-9.4 GB as before. WHAT DID NOT HAPPEN, and a later author must not read it as closed: the WholeCompilerRebuildRequired PartitionGenerationAuthorityChanged arm never fired, and behind it admit_derived_partition_move, partition_move_explanation_child and the boundary_fold phase -- partition_move appears in the log only inside the partition_moved=false field. The reason is mechanical, and it is written here precisely because two earlier readings of this very run got it wrong in opposite directions. The seven *_today functions in dag/gunbc/stage0_partition_rebuild_scope.dag WERE evaluated at every stage: partition_rebuild_actuation builds its arguments and calls decider.evaluate DIRECTLY, and parent.decision.begin is printed by exactly one other site in the stage0 crate, rebuild_scope_decision_with, which that closure bypasses -- so their evaluation leaves no trace line, and the absence of the line was never evidence of absence. The run's own output shows the evaluation reached PR #16373's code: the line naming owning_packages=[v1-compiler, v1-stage0-v1-infer] is the return of stage0_partition_rebuild_decision_line_today, which passes rows: generated_partition_crate_rows_as_declared(), and a package roster like that can only come from the declared fold. What the stage never did was move a mirror named in data rebuild_scope_partition_generation_mirrors, which is exactly two paths, gunbc_stage0_stage0_crate_partition_generated.rs and v1_compiler_stage0_crates.rs; without that intersection the decision cannot be PartitionGenerationAuthorityChanged, so moved stayed false and the admission behind it was never reached. Corrected on bold-wren-111's retraction of their own msg_147f66c0 and msg_cf50a775 (their msg_e435a871), and re-verified in this tree at this head rather than accepted from anyone. SECOND: the generated carrier never received the row -- stage0_crate_partition_generated.dag still had 0 rest_cause_text rows and its .rs mirror stayed at the base blob ec5a4c11 where main holds 4f3feac2 -- and heal reported NO drift on either. That is not a hole this round is dropping, and a later author needs the reason rather than the symptom. The round this row covers is heal.yml's FIRST step, claim_executor --regen-round-cost --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope, which is what ppf-16373 and ppf-16377 ran. The carrier .dag is written by heal.yml's SECOND step, which runs dag/gunbc/heal_candidate_stage0.dag heal_tail_wet: it first refuses if the stage0 round touched any seed-build path (HealStage0RoundWroteSeedBuildArtifact), then folds seed_build_artifacts() through main_wet imported from gunbc.instruments.seed_build_artifacts_regen -- NOT gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate, whose roster reaches the same body only through gunbc.generated_artifact_emit seed_build_outcome -- writing each row with read-back. Its content is expected_stage0_crate_partition_generated_dag over stage0_partition_crate_rows() from v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition, the same partition authority this PR routes the crate roots through, so the carrier has ONE authority and is simply not this round's to write. WHAT IS NOT COVERED, and this is the constraint the next author meets (bold-wren-111 msg_d177c22d, read from main 59dde49a, nothing built): heal REPAIRS the carrier, it does not compare it, and heal is not a required context -- v2-bootstrap runs no emit or gate step at all, and heal.yml's own trigger is a path list on a same-repo PR -- so a fork, a cancelled heal, or a merge that lands before heal publishes leaves the carrier behind its authored rows with nothing on the required path noticing. And the carrier .rs is a stage0 mirror, which the round owns rather than the seed-build writer: its content follows the .dag, which the round reads BEFORE that second step rewrites it, so a single heal pass can leave the mirror one round behind its carrier -- that last part is bold-wren-111's inference from the step order and NOT an observation, and the specimen that adds a partition PACKAGE rather than a module is the one that would settle it. RUNG: stays at mechanically preventable, and the reason is stated in the trigger capability rather than left to inference. DEFECT 2 RESIDUAL, named as a follow-up and NOT taken here: aa761c29cfe3 (#14340) already carries the payload, but the host match on regen_stage_plan_kind_label has arms only for the three planned kinds, so a legitimate refusal is reported as refusal: convergence kind projection returned unknown closed variant Refused: <detail> -- the right location in the wrong class, and a fourth arm would classify it. THIRD, a weakness in this PR's own guard, recorded because a pin that cannot fail is worse than no pin: the new claim counts the NAME boundary_outcome_from_declared_partition in the boundary host and one of its three occurrences at head is in a doc comment, so a comment-only edit with no behaviour change can redden it; the mutation run (quick-newt-573 msg_a3ffec50, scratch /tmp/qn-mut, discarded) put the snapshot authority back and got 24 PASS 1 FAIL with the FAIL on exactly that arm, which is what gives the pin its teeth. Tightening it to count the call form instead of the name is a one-line follow-up.",
